# GitHub Actions FTP deploy (no SSH / no cPanel Terminal)
#
# === Secrets (Settings → Secrets → Actions) ===
# FTP_SERVER, FTP_USERNAME, FTP_PASSWORD, FTP_SERVER_DIR  (trailing slash, e.g. /public_html/ispbilling/)
# DEPLOY_EXTRACT_TOKEN  — long random string for browser extract URL
# Optional: FTP_PORT (21), FTP_PROTOCOL (ftp or ftps)
#
# === Two workflows ===
#
# 1) "Deploy to production (FTP)" — runs on every push to main
#    Uploads app code + assets only (fast). Does NOT upload vendor.
#
# 2) "Upload vendor (FTP chunks)" — run MANUALLY from Actions tab
#    When: first deploy, or after composer.lock changes
#    Uploads vendor in 5 MB chunks (works on slow FTP hosts)
#    Then open in browser:
#      https://YOUR-DOMAIN/deploy-extract-vendor.php?token=YOUR_TOKEN
#
# === Manual alternative (no GitHub vendor upload) ===
#    On your PC:  .\scripts\build-vendor-zip.ps1
#    cPanel File Manager → upload vendor.zip → Extract → delete zip
#
# Document root must point to public/ inside this Laravel app.
